Subject: [PATCH 53/63] [cuttlefish] Add instance registry library
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Summary:
# Motivation:
Developers running multiple emulator types simultaneously on macOS need independently-launched Cuttlefish instances to coexist. The existing single global config symlink only supports one launch_cvd invocation at a time, and the monolithic launch/stop model requires all instances to be managed together.

# Overview:
Add a new instance registry library (instance_registry.h/.cpp) that tracks
independently-launched Cuttlefish instances via a shared JSON file
(/tmp/cuttlefish_instances_<uid>.json).

The registry supports:
- RegisterInstance / UnregisterInstance for lifecycle management
- LookupInstance / ListInstances for querying state
- ClaimNextFreeInstance for atomic instance number assignment
- IsInstanceRunning / GetInstanceConfigPath convenience helpers

Concurrent access is protected by flock() and writes are atomic
(write-to-temp + rename). Stale entries (dead PIDs) are cleaned up
automatically during ListInstances and ClaimNextFreeInstance.

No consumers yet; subsequent commits will wire this into assemble_cvd,
launch_cvd, and stop_cvd.

```
  Registry library API (this commit):

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │          instance_registry.h/.cpp                │
  │                                                  │
  │  RegisterInstance(num, config_path, pid)          │
  │  UnregisterInstance(num)                          │
  │  LookupInstance(num) -> optional<Entry>           │
  │  ListInstances() -> vector<Entry>  [cleans stale]│
  │  ClaimNextFreeInstance(start) -> int              │
  │  IsInstanceRunning(num) -> bool                  │
  │  GetInstanceConfigPath(num) -> string            │
  └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘
                         │ flock() + atomic write
                         v
    /tmp/cuttlefish_instances_<uid>.json
    {
      "instances": {
        "1": { "config_path": "...", "run_cvd_pid": 100, "status": "running" },
        "2": { "config_path": "...", "run_cvd_pid": 200, "status": "running" }
      }
    }

  Intended usage (subsequent commits):

  launch_cvd (phone)    launch_cvd (watch)
       |                     |
       v                     v
  assemble_cvd           assemble_cvd
    ClaimNextFreeInstance   ClaimNextFreeInstance
    RegisterInstance         RegisterInstance
       |                     |
       v                     v
  run_cvd (pid 100)     run_cvd (pid 200)

  stop_cvd --instance_num=1     stop_cvd (no args)
       |                             |
       v                             v
  LookupInstance(1)             ListInstances()
  stop + UnregisterInstance     stop all + UnregisterInstance
```

